      "extract": "THE SQUARING OPERATION FOR COMMUTATIVE DG RINGS AMNON YEKUTIELI Abstract. Let A →B be a homomorphism of commutative rings. The squar- ing operation is a functor SqB/A from the derived category D(B) of complexes of B-modules into itself. This operation is needed for the deﬁnition of rigid complexes (in the sense of Van den Bergh), that in turn leads to a new approach to Grothendieck duality for rings, schemes and",
